// Paragraphs labelled for the second batch of construct questions (inkling judge), scored with `judges/jev/calibrate_constructs.py --batch 2`. `q` is the question, `yes` the label, `rule` the regex rule whose fail example it rephrases (`orig` marks the rule's own example), `before` the paragraph Jev sees as context, `mode` the inkling mode. Every case is also a no for the other batch-2 questions it is not labelled for.
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": "narrator/tense-match", "mode": "post", "yes": true, "text": "Models are biased towards text that models wrote.", "before": "", "orig": true, "id": "tense_mismatch-0"}
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": "narrator/tense-match", "mode": "post", "yes": true, "text": "Readers trust posts that people wrote more than generated ones.", "before": "", "orig": true, "id": "tense_mismatch-1"}
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": "narrator/tense-match", "mode": "post", "yes": true, "text": "Judges prefer answers that a model produced over ones a person typed.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "tense_mismatch-2"}
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": "narrator/tense-match", "mode": "post", "yes": true, "text": "Engineers trusted dashboards that showed tokens, as a rule.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "tense_mismatch-3"}
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": "narrator/tense-match", "mode": "post", "yes": true, "text": "Yesterday my agent opens the trace, reads the error and sends a fix, and then it goes back and checks again.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "tense_mismatch-4"}
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": "narrator/tense-match", "mode": "post", "yes": true, "text": "On 8 November the writer drafts the post, the judge flags two lines and the writer rewrites them.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "tense_mismatch-5"}
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": null, "mode": "post", "yes": false, "text": "Researchers at Meta found the judges picked text that models wrote.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "tense_mismatch-6"}
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": null, "mode": "post", "yes": false, "text": "The email that Ana wrote was short.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "tense_mismatch-7"}
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": null, "mode": "post", "yes": false, "text": "Models are biased towards text that other models write.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "tense_mismatch-8"}
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": null, "mode": "post", "yes": false, "text": "On 8 November the writer drafted the post, the judge flagged two lines and the writer rewrote them.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "tense_mismatch-9"}
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": null, "mode": "post", "yes": false, "text": "Every morning the agent opens the queue and answers the oldest ticket first.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "tense_mismatch-10"}
{"q": "tense_mismatch", "rule": null, "mode": "post", "yes": false, "text": "When a release ships, the handoff rate moves first.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "tense_mismatch-11"}
{"q": "lecture_turn", "rule": "structure/lecture-turn", "mode": "post", "yes": true, "text": "LLMs regress to the mean, so an agent that edits itself drifts toward generic behaviour.", "before": "If you build agents, you probably run this loop by hand.", "orig": true, "id": "lecture_turn-12"}
{"q": "lecture_turn", "rule": "structure/lecture-turn", "mode": "post", "yes": true, "text": "Language models are trained to please, which is why self-editing agents converge on bland output.", "before": "You've probably asked your agent to fix its own prompt at least once.", "orig": false, "id": "lecture_turn-13"}
{"q": "lecture_turn", "rule": "structure/lecture-turn", "mode": "post", "yes": true, "text": "Agents, as a class, tend to forget instructions after a long context.", "before": "If your agent ran overnight, you know the feeling of reading its log in the morning.", "orig": false, "id": "lecture_turn-14"}
{"q": "lecture_turn", "rule": "structure/lecture-turn", "mode": "post", "yes": true, "text": "AI systems optimise for what they are measured on.", "before": "You can ship a new prompt every day if you want to.", "orig": false, "id": "lecture_turn-15"}
{"q": "lecture_turn", "rule": null, "mode": "post", "yes": false, "text": "By now you might have been tempted to let another agent improve yours, but LLMs regress to the mean.", "before": "If you build agents, you probably run this loop by hand.", "orig": false, "id": "lecture_turn-16"}
{"q": "lecture_turn", "rule": null, "mode": "post", "yes": false, "text": "LLMs regress to the mean, so we measure every change.", "before": "We built the loop in two weeks.", "orig": false, "id": "lecture_turn-17"}
{"q": "lecture_turn", "rule": null, "mode": "post", "yes": false, "text": "Your agent will forget the plan after a long context, so we write the plan to a file.", "before": "If your agent ran overnight, you know the feeling of reading its log in the morning.", "orig": false, "id": "lecture_turn-18"}
{"q": "lecture_turn", "rule": null, "mode": "post", "yes": false, "text": "That's why I check its prompt before every release.", "before": "You've probably asked your agent to fix its own prompt at least once.", "orig": false, "id": "lecture_turn-19"}
{"q": "overclaim", "rule": "narrator/overclaim", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "The root cause is that code has a judge, and writing doesn't. Without that judge, our research found six main ways AI writing goes wrong.", "before": "", "orig": true, "id": "overclaim-20"}
{"q": "overclaim", "rule": "narrator/overclaim", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "The real reason agents fail is missing context. The second reason is a weak prompt, and the third is no evals.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "overclaim-21"}
{"q": "overclaim", "rule": "narrator/overclaim", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "There's really only one thing behind it: no tests. Then there's the prompt, the model choice and the missing traces too.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "overclaim-22"}
{"q": "overclaim", "rule": "narrator/overclaim", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "What it all comes down to is the judge. We found five more causes after that.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "overclaim-23"}
{"q": "overclaim", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The first reason, and the root of the others, is that code has a judge. Our research found six main ways AI writing goes wrong.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "overclaim-24"}
{"q": "overclaim", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The root cause is a missing index.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "overclaim-25"}
{"q": "overclaim", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "One reason agents fail is missing context. Another is a weak prompt.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "overclaim-26"}
{"q": "overclaim", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The bug came down to one thing: a cache key without the user id.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "overclaim-27"}
{"q": "overclaim", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "We found three causes: missing context, a weak prompt and no evals.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "overclaim-28"}
{"q": "overclaim", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The main cost is the model call, and the rest is storage.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "overclaim-29"}
