{"q": "dangling_reference", "rule": "script/dangling-back-reference", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "A smaller version is writing from the middle of a conversation.", "before": "The model fills every gap with what it already knows.", "orig": true, "id": "dangling_reference-151"}
{"q": "dangling_reference", "rule": "script/dangling-back-reference", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "This is hard even for humans.", "before": "The model lists features.", "orig": true, "id": "dangling_reference-152"}
{"q": "dangling_reference", "rule": "script/dangling-back-reference", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "That makes it worse when the reader is new.", "before": "We looked at three posts the founder rejected last week, and each one had a different problem.", "orig": false, "id": "dangling_reference-153"}
{"q": "dangling_reference", "rule": "script/dangling-back-reference", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "The same thing happens with titles.", "before": "Sometimes the agent writes for the wrong reader, sometimes it crams, and sometimes it hedges.", "orig": false, "id": "dangling_reference-154"}
{"q": "dangling_reference", "rule": "script/dangling-back-reference", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "It gets even stranger in the second case.", "before": "Let's look at how agents write landing pages.", "orig": false, "id": "dangling_reference-155"}
{"q": "dangling_reference", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "What you may have noticed is that the model writes from the middle of a conversation.", "before": "The model fills every gap with what it already knows.", "orig": false, "id": "dangling_reference-156"}
{"q": "dangling_reference", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "This is a short lesson on how agents write.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "dangling_reference-157"}
{"q": "dangling_reference", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "Listing features is hard to avoid, even for people.", "before": "The model lists features.", "orig": false, "id": "dangling_reference-158"}
{"q": "dangling_reference", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The same thing happens with titles: the model crams three claims into one line.", "before": "The model crams three claims into one sentence.", "orig": false, "id": "dangling_reference-159"}
{"q": "dangling_reference", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "That's why we test with readers who know nothing.", "before": "Our agent knows everything about the product, so it skips what a newcomer needs.", "orig": false, "id": "dangling_reference-160"}
{"q": "elegant_variation", "rule": "script/elegant-variation", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "The model predicts the next word. And the AI drifts to the average. The system never surprises.", "before": "", "orig": true, "id": "elegant_variation-161"}
{"q": "elegant_variation", "rule": "script/elegant-variation", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "We decide who reads it. Next, we write the tests. After that, we write the draft.", "before": "", "orig": true, "id": "elegant_variation-162"}
{"q": "elegant_variation", "rule": "script/elegant-variation", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "The agent reads the ticket. Then the assistant looks up the order, and the bot writes the reply.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "elegant_variation-163"}
{"q": "elegant_variation", "rule": "script/elegant-variation", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "Our checker reads the draft. The linter flags two lines, and the tool suggests a fix.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "elegant_variation-164"}
{"q": "elegant_variation", "rule": "script/elegant-variation", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "Customers open the app. Users pick a project, and clients see their traces.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "elegant_variation-165"}
{"q": "elegant_variation", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The model predicts the next word. And the model drifts to the average, and the model never surprises you.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "elegant_variation-166"}
{"q": "elegant_variation", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "We decide who reads it. Then we write the tests, and then we write the draft.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "elegant_variation-167"}
{"q": "elegant_variation", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The agent reads the ticket, looks up the order and writes the reply.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "elegant_variation-168"}
{"q": "elegant_variation", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The judge reads the draft and the readers answer the questions.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "elegant_variation-169"}
{"q": "elegant_variation", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "Customers open the app and pick a project.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "elegant_variation-170"}
{"q": "elegant_variation", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The linter flags two lines, and the judge flags one more.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "elegant_variation-171"}
{"q": "colon_list", "rule": "script/colon-list", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "You picture what's in their head: what they know, what they want and what they care about.", "before": "", "orig": true, "id": "colon_list-172"}
{"q": "colon_list", "rule": "script/colon-list", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "A good title has three things: a claim, a reader and a surprise.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "colon_list-173"}
{"q": "colon_list", "rule": "script/colon-list", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "Think about your reader: their job, their worry and their next step.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "colon_list-174"}
{"q": "colon_list", "rule": "script/colon-list", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "It comes down to this: context, contrast and craft.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "colon_list-175"}
{"q": "colon_list", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "You see their face drop, and you start over in simpler words.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "colon_list-176"}
{"q": "colon_list", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "It's the same at work: a test fails, a screenshot looks wrong, and I fix it.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "colon_list-177"}
{"q": "colon_list", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "Here's the one thing that matters: who reads it.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "colon_list-178"}
{"q": "colon_list", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The agent needs a key: the one from your project settings.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "colon_list-179"}
{"q": "colon_list", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "We support three languages, Python, TypeScript and Go, and more are coming.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "colon_list-180"}
{"q": "colon_list", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "You picture the reader and what they want from the page.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "colon_list-181"}
{"q": "aside_jump", "rule": "script/aside-jump", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "The model drifts to the middle, which statisticians call regression to the mean.", "before": "", "orig": true, "id": "aside_jump-182"}
{"q": "aside_jump", "rule": "script/aside-jump", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "Readers already know too much, a bias psychologists have named the curse of knowledge.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "aside_jump-183"}
{"q": "aside_jump", "rule": "script/aside-jump", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "The judge likes its own text, what researchers call self-preference bias.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "aside_jump-184"}
{"q": "aside_jump", "rule": "script/aside-jump", "mode": "script", "yes": true, "text": "It picks the likely word, known in the field as greedy decoding.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "aside_jump-185"}
{"q": "aside_jump", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The model drifts to the middle. Statisticians have a name for this: regression to the mean.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "aside_jump-186"}
{"q": "aside_jump", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The judge likes its own text, which is why we calibrate it on lines people approved.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "aside_jump-187"}
{"q": "aside_jump", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "It picks the most likely word every time.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "aside_jump-188"}
{"q": "aside_jump", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "Psychologists call it the curse of knowledge, and it's why experts write badly for beginners.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "aside_jump-189"}
{"q": "aside_jump", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "The model drifts to the middle when nothing pulls it out.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "aside_jump-190"}
{"q": "aside_jump", "rule": null, "mode": "script", "yes": false, "text": "Readers already know too much about our product, so they skip the basics.", "before": "", "orig": false, "id": "aside_jump-191"}
{"q": "docs_scene_opener", "rule": "docs/indefinite-event-opener", "mode": "docs", "yes": true, "text": "A developer connects the agent to the platform once.", "before": "", "orig": true, "id": "docs_scene_opener-192"}
